From 091191ef68191c2925b8ac7123c10fe453c577d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for Zenbook A16 owner)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] arm64: efi: Power off the ASUS Zenbook A16 through PSCI

The ASUS Zenbook A16 (UX3607OA) reboots when Linux powers it off
through the UEFI ResetSystem() runtime service: systemd logs
"System is powering down" and the next boot starts a second later.
Skip the EFI power-off handler on it, as on the Inspiron 14 3420, so
PSCI SYSTEM_OFF turns it off.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c
index fc81e9a4a..e37ceb4a8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c
@@ -158,8 +158,9 @@ int __init efi_set_mapping_permissions(struct mm_struct *mm,
  */
 bool efi_poweroff_required(void)
 {
-	/* Its ResetSystem(EfiResetShutdown) reboots instead */
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("dell,inspiron-3420-sc8180xp"))
+	/* Their ResetSystem(EfiResetShutdown) reboots instead */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("dell,inspiron-3420-sc8180xp") ||
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenbook-a16-ux3607oa"))
 		return false;
 
 	return efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES);
-- 
